<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- NuGet package metadata (discoverability) -->
    <PackageId>STAF.LLMEval</PackageId>
    <Version>2.0.1</Version>
    <Title>STAF.LLMEval — .NET LLM Evaluation and AI Testing Framework</Title>
    <Authors>Sooraj Ramachandran</Authors>
    <Company>Sooraj Ramachandran</Company>
    <Product>STAF.LLMEval</Product>
    <Description>STAF.LLMEval is a .NET library and AI testing framework for evaluating LLM and GenAI responses in unit tests and CI/CD. Score AI outputs with exact match, keyword overlap, TF-IDF semantic similarity, LLM-as-judge, and RAG groundedness / hallucination detection. Includes fluent Eval API, assertions (ShouldPass, ShouldBeGrounded), Options/DI, JSON/JSONL evaluation suites, and HTML/JSON reports. Works with OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, Google Gemini, and Ollama. Ideal for ChatGPT/GPT evaluation, RAG quality checks, golden-dataset regression, and automated AI response validation on .NET 8/9/10.</Description>
    <PackageTags>LLM;LLM-evaluation;LLM-as-judge;AI;AI-evaluation;AI-testing;GenAI;generative-AI;ChatGPT;GPT;OpenAI;Azure-OpenAI;AzureOpenAI;Gemini;Ollama;RAG;RAG-evaluation;grounding;groundedness;hallucination;hallucination-detection;semantic-similarity;TF-IDF;exact-match;golden-dataset;evaluation-suite;AI-assertions;unit-testing;xUnit;MSTest;NUnit;CI-CD;dotnet;net8;net9;net10;fluent-API;AI-response-evaluation;prompt-evaluation;model-evaluation;quality-assurance;QA;testing-framework;STAF</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
STAF.LLMEval 2.0.1 — Metadata and discoverability update (same APIs as 2.0.0)

- Richer NuGet title, description, and search tags (LLM evaluation, RAG, hallucination, AI testing, etc.)
- Expanded PackageReleaseNotes and README wording for NuGet / Google / AI search discovery
- No breaking API changes from 2.0.0

2.0.0 Adoption features (included):
- Multi-target net8.0/net9.0/net10.0; Eval.Direct/Judge/Grounding; assertions; AddLLMEval; JSON/JSONL suites + HTML/JSON reports; Azure OpenAI
- Classic EvaluationRequest / EvaluateAsync remain compatible
See https://github.com/sooraj171/LLMEval/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/sooraj171/LLMEval</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/sooraj171/LLMEval</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <Copyright>Copyright © Sooraj Ramachandran 2026</Copyright>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="Readme.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="README.md" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="8.0.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Http" Version="8.0.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" Version="8.0.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
